=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_f4a7 — Thursday Guest Evening: Dinner at Six, Games After

Marco and Yuki have told the robot that friends are coming over Thursday evening. This is a one-off social event that overrides the normal weekday rhythm for the afternoon and evening of that day. Marco, who is normally out from 14:00 to 23:00 on weekdays, will be home by 17:00 to help set the table and greet guests. Yuki will be in the kitchen from mid-afternoon preparing a proper dinner rather than her usual light meal. The dinner is served at the kitchen table around 18:00–19:30, after which the group moves to the living room for conversation, a board game, and perhaps a second round of drinks. The candle on the coffee table is lit for the occasion. The remote is set aside on the coffee table rather than left on the TV stand, because the evening is for talking and playing, not watching. The dog gets an extra bowl of food before the guests arrive so it is settled and quiet during dinner. The blanket is pulled onto the couch for comfort.

What sets this document apart: it is the only hypothesis that places Marco home by 17:00 on a weekday, that puts the serving dish and extra plates at the kitchen table in the 17:00–20:00 window, that moves the board game to the coffee table, and that removes the remote from the TV stand. A standard weekday document would have Marco's keys out of the house until 23:00, the serving dish in the cupboard, the board game on the bookshelf, and the remote on the TV stand.

What would refute it: if Marco's keys are still out of the house at 18:00 (he did not come home early); if the serving dish is found in the cupboard during the 17:00–20:00 window; if the remote is on the TV stand at 20:00 (they are watching TV, not socializing); if the board game is on the bookshelf at 20:00.

