# p_9c3e — Marco Journals at the Bedroom Desk, Not the Nightstand

The sightings tell a clear story about Marco's journal: at 03:00 it is on the nightstand, at 12:00 it is at the bedroom desk (seen twice), and at 18:00 it is back on the nightstand. The per-object evidence confirms this: weekday 9–17 h looks at the nightstand found the journal 0 times and found nothing 2 times, meaning it is NOT on the nightstand during the day. The journal lives at the desk_b1 during waking hours and is returned to the nightstand at night. Marco is a journaler who works at his desk during the afternoon (before his shift, or on weekends), and the journal sits with his notebook and book at the desk while he works. At night he moves it to the nightstand for a last entry before bed.

This document corrects the nightstand-during-the-day claim that p_b7c2 made and that has been scored against twice. The journal is at the bedroom desk from roughly 08:00 to 20:00 on weekdays, and on the nightstand outside that window.

What sets this apart: it is the only document that places journal_marco at desk_b1 during the 08:00–20:00 weekday window. Documents that put it on the nightstand all day will be contradicted by the 12:00 desk sightings.

What would refute it: if the journal is found on the nightstand at 12:00 or 14:00 on a weekday, or if it is found at the office desk (desk_o1) rather than the bedroom desk.

