# p_5d8b — The Dog Food Bag Lives on the Kitchen Floor

The mixture's worst prediction is the dog food bag: it was predicted at pantry_shelf_k1 but actually found at floor_k_k1 five times. The sightings confirm this: 03:00 floor_k_k1, 07:00 floor_k_k1, 08:00 floor_k_k1 (x2), 18:00 pantry_shelf_k1, 22:00 floor_k_k1 (x2) and pantry_shelf_k1 (x1). The bag sits on the kitchen floor next to the dog bowl for daily feeding, and is only moved to the pantry shelf briefly when Yuki is tidying up or doing a larger refill. The per-object evidence shows the bag at floor_k_k1 on 1 of 2 sighted days as the "mostly" location, but the raw sightings are 6 of 8 on the floor. The bag is a working tool: it is opened, used, and left on the floor where the dog eats.

This document corrects the pantry-shelf default that the statistical model and several other documents use. The bag is on the kitchen floor from 06:00 to 20:00 on weekdays (covering both feedings and the midday top-up), and only goes to the pantry in the early morning before the first feeding or during an evening tidy-up.

What sets this apart: it is the only document that places dog_food_bag_shared at floor_k_k1 as the primary resting spot during the day. Documents that default it to the pantry will be contradicted by the repeated floor sightings.

What would refute it: if the bag is consistently found in the pantry during the 07:00–19:00 window on multiple days, or if it is found in the storage room.

